# Jira connection
error-jira-access-denied = Jira says you don't have permission to do that.
error-jira-action-key-used = That action has already been carried out in Jira.
error-jira-address-invalid = That isn't a valid Jira address. Use the secure address of your Atlassian site.
error-jira-issue-type-none = This Jira project has no suitable kind of issue to create. Choose another project.
error-jira-not-connected = You haven't connected Jira yet. Connect it and try again.
error-jira-not-found = Jira couldn't find that. It may have been moved or deleted.
error-jira-outcome-unknown = Jira may have received your comment or issue, but no answer came back. Check Jira before trying again.
error-jira-query-invalid = Jira couldn't understand that search. Check what you typed and try again.
error-jira-response-invalid = Jira gave an answer ordin couldn't read. Try again in a moment.
error-jira-sign-in-needed = Sign in to Jira again.
error-jira-site-mismatch = That refers to a different Jira site from the one you connected.
error-jira-throttled = Jira is busy and asked ordin to slow down. Try again in a moment.
error-jira-token-refused = Jira didn't accept those sign-in details. Check them and try again.
error-jira-too-large = That is too large for Jira. Shorten the text or use a smaller attachment.
error-jira-unavailable = Jira can't be reached right now. Try again in a moment.
